<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Sanjar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad Sanjar was a Seljuk sultan who ruled from Khurasan in the first half of the twelfth century, the last ruler to hold authority over much of the Great Seljuk realm. His defeat by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qatwan">Battle of Qatwan</a> in 1141 and his later capture by Oghuz tribes weakened the dynasty. His death in 1157 is often treated as the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Great Seljuk Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmad-sanjar.jpg" alt="Ahmad Sanjar" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rashid Al-Din · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahmad_Sanjar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
